   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Frame in frame 2\n\n1. **Viewer**: facade 40 m wide, audience 15 m in front, centred, eye 1.7 m (estimated from the site photos).\n2. **Region Plan**: per region `fif_depth_m` (m behind the facade; < 0 = sticks out), `fif_source` =\n   `generate` | `media` | `world`, `fif_media` = a name from media_names or an index (empty = in turn).\n3. **Frame Compose** draws every frame as the viewer sees it: generate = perspective guide, media = your\n   image on the back wall, world = one image behind the whole facade. Region Sampler then paints the\n   generate frames (denoise 0.95, reference self keeps the perspective).\n4. From 15 m you look steeply up: on upper floors deep rooms show mostly ceiling. Keep depths shallow there\n   (0.3-0.5 m = a picture just behind the glass, a window reveal onto the world).\n5. Negative depth = a parasite sticking out (here the ground floor side windows, 1.5 m) with a shadow on the\n   facade; Frame Compose's `plan` output (with the parasites as <name>_out regions) goes to the sampler.\n\nMedia: the three Load Image nodes use ComfyUI's own example.png; pick others; the two media\nimages are scaled to the same size for the batch.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  },
